  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper demonstrates three small-scale quantum finance prototypes on IBM 5‑qubit processors: (1) quantum Monte Carlo risk metrics using 4–5 qubits and 8192 shots, (2) HHL-based portfolio optimization requiring circuits up to ~13,762 gates that fail on real hardware, and (3) a 5‑qubit QAOA portfolio selection problem where the correct solution is found but only for a toy 5‑asset instance. All practical results show strong hardware noise limitations, and no quantum advantage is demonstrated.",
